      "notes": "Module models the 2440 lb Warrior II (TCDS Item XVI-B, S/N 28-8316001+; engine O-320-D3G), so the certified CG envelope is Item XVI-B Normal Category (NOTE 26): (+83.0) to (+93.0) at 1950 lb or less; (+88.3) to (+93.0) at 2440 lb (straight-line variation). Module was a near-flat forward limit 83.0 rising only to 84.0 at 2440 lb -> up to 4.3 in MORE nose-heavy-permissive than certified at gross (FD-413 forward-limit-taper defect). Aft limit 93.0 already correct. Station arms front 80.5 / rear 118.1 / baggage 142.8 (200 lb at +142.8) / fuel 95.0 (50 gal at +95) all confirmed CORRECT against TCDS Item XVI-B 'No. of Seats Normal Category: 4 (2 at +80.5, 2 at +118.1)'. (The earlier 2325 lb Warrior II, Item XVI-A, uses +87.0 at 2325 lb — not this module.) DEFERRED (Track B): empty_weight/empty_weight_arm nominal (TCDS Empty Weight C.G. Range: None); usable_fuel_gal 48 vs TCDS 50 gal total; the takeoff-obstacle over-50 rows (TO_OVER50_RATIO_FD419) are a Track-B perf fix. Full findings: docs/fd-419-s2-piper-singles-wb-findings-2026-07-26.md."
